From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cristian Papa <pcristian292@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 14:21:21 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 48/48] net: xpon: omci: ignore an extended OMCC version
 instead of failing

"stay on the baseline message set" refused the OMCC version code points
that announce the extended message set with -EINVAL. The OMCI agent
configuration applies its keys one by one and stops at the first error,
so such a value also left the hardware and software versions and the
reboot policy that follow it unapplied.

Keep the current OMCC version and warn instead, so that only that one
value is ignored.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 net/xpon/omci/agent.c | 14 +++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/net/xpon/omci/agent.c b/net/xpon/omci/agent.c
index 3a83581..0c2ff80 100644
--- a/net/xpon/omci/agent.c
+++ b/net/xpon/omci/agent.c
@@ -5532,10 +5532,22 @@ __omci_agent_config_set_source(struct omci_device *odev, u16 key,
 			break;
 		}
 		scalar = *(const u8 *)value;
-		if (!scalar || omci_omcc_version_extended(scalar)) {
+		if (!scalar) {
 			ret = -EINVAL;
 			break;
 		}
+		/*
+		 * The agent only speaks the baseline message set. Ignore a
+		 * code point that announces the extended one, but do not fail:
+		 * a configuration applies its keys in order and would stop
+		 * before the hardware and software versions.
+		 */
+		if (omci_omcc_version_extended(scalar)) {
+			dev_warn(odev->parent,
+				 "OMCC version %#04x announces the extended message set, ignored (keeping %#04x)\n",
+				 scalar, agent->config.omcc_version);
+			break;
+		}
 		changed = agent->config.omcc_version != scalar;
 		agent->config.omcc_version = scalar;
 		agent->config.omcc_version_source = source;
